  "live_records": {
    "q-214997": {
      "dom_id": "step-q214997",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is $73\\,\\text{kg}$ expressed in $\\text{g}?$ Write your answer as a whole number.\n\n$73\\,\\text{kg}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\text{g}$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by recalling the conversion table for mass units. \n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilogram | $\\text{kg}$ | $1\\,\\text{kg}=1\\,000\\,\\text{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\text{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\text{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\text{mg}=1\\,\\text{g}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThere are $1000\\,\\text{g}$ per $\\text{kg},$ which we can write as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1000\\,\\text{g}}{\\text{kg}}\n$$\n\nThis is our conversion factor.\n\nNow, multiplying $73\\,\\text{kg}$ by our conversion factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}73\\,\\text{kg} & =73\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{g}}{\\text{kg}} \\\\  & =73\\,\\cancel{\\text{kg}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{g}}{\\cancel{\\text{kg}}} \\\\  & =73\\cdot 1\\,000\\,\\text{g} \\\\  & =73\\,000\\,\\text{g}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $73\\,\\text{kg}$ is equivalent to $73\\,000\\,\\text{g}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
