    "q-215007": {
      "dom_id": "step-q215007",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is $4\\,\\text{g}$ expressed in $\\text{mg}?$ Write your answer as a whole number.\n\n$4\\,\\text{g}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\text{mg}$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by recalling the conversion table for mass units. \n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilogram | $\\text{kg}$ | $1\\,\\text{kg}=1\\,000\\,\\text{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\text{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\text{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\text{mg}=1\\,\\text{g}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThere are $1000\\,\\text{mg}$ per $\\text{g},$ which we can write as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1000\\,\\text{mg}}{\\text{g}}\n$$\n\nThis is our conversion factor.\n\nNow, multiplying $4\\,\\text{g}$ by our conversion factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\,\\text{g} & =4\\,\\text{g}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{mg}}{\\text{g}} \\\\  & =4\\,\\cancel{\\text{g}}\\cdot \\frac{1\\,000\\,\\text{mg}}{\\cancel{\\text{g}}} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1\\,000\\,\\text{mg} \\\\  & =4\\,000\\,\\text{mg}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4\\,\\text{g}$ is equivalent to $4\\,000\\,\\text{mg}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
