    "q-144483": {
      "dom_id": "step-q144483",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is $4\\,250\\,\\text{g}$ expressed in $\\text{kg}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We start by recalling the conversion table for mass units. \n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Kilogram | $\\text{kg}$ | $1\\,\\text{kg}=1\\,000\\,\\text{g}$ |\n| Gram | $\\text{g}$ | Base Unit |\n| Milligram | $\\text{mg}$ | $1\\,000\\,\\text{mg}=1\\,\\text{g}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThere are $1000\\,\\text{g}$ per $\\text{kg},$ which we can write as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1000\\,\\text{g}}{\\text{kg}}\n$$\n\nHowever, since we're converting from a smaller unit of mass $(\\text{g})$ to a larger one $(\\text{kg}),$ we need to multiply $4\\,250\\,\\text{g}$ by the reciprocal of the above:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{kg}}{1000\\,\\text{g}}\n$$\n\nThis is our conversion factor.\n\nNow, multiplying $4\\,250\\,\\text{g}$ by our conversion factor, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\,250\\,\\text{g} & =4\\,250\\,\\text{g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{kg}}{1000\\,\\text{g}} \\\\  & =4\\,250\\,\\cancel{\\text{g}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{kg}}{1000\\,\\cancel{\\text{g}}} \\\\  & =4\\,250\\cdot \\frac{\\text{kg}}{1000} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\,250}{1\\,000}\\,\\text{kg} \\\\  & =4.25\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4\\,250\\,\\text{g}$ is equivalent to $4.25\\,\\text{kg}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
